      "flags": {},
      "order": 6,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# IMAGE -> TEXT (detailed description)\n\nTurns any image into a rich natural-language description, ready to paste into the Krea 2 (or any Qwen-family) prompt.\n\n## Chain\nLoadImage (SOURCE IMAGE) -> [VL toggle] -> TextGenerate (describe system prompt + image) -> description text.\n\n## VL toggle (which vision model describes)\n- **Flux: OFF / Qwen: ON** (default Flux = 4B).\n- Flux (OFF) = **qwen3vl_4b** (the Krea 2 text encoder, type krea2). Fast, always loaded with your gen stack. Good descriptions.\n- Qwen (ON) = **qwen3vl_32b minimax_h3** (nvfp4). The bigger VL - noticeably better/more detailed descriptions, slower and heavier (12+ GB, streams).\n- Lazy: only the selected VL runs.\n\n## Usage\n- Pick your image in LoadImage, Queue.\n- The description appears as text ON the TextGenerate node output - select and copy it.\n- Paste it into the Krea 2 workflow's IDEA node (or use the consistency workflow which does this automatically).\n- The description prompt (PrimitiveStringMultiline) is editable - tighten it for specific needs (e.g. \"describe only the person, ignore background\").\n\n## Why this works with Krea 2\n- The Qwen-Image family conditions on Qwen3-VL - these models genuinely prefer long, natural-language, Qwen-written prompts over tag soup. A VL-written description is the native prompt style."
      ]
    },
